    <string name="ona_overlay_output">Where the input goes</string>
    <string name="ona_overlay_backend_touch">No root: keys + touch</string>
    <string name="ona_overlay_backend_touch_summary">Letter keys, ESC, Enter, Shift… go to the app in front like a keyboard (Android 13+). Buttons set to TAP touch their point, TOUCH_DRAG sticks move the app\'s own stick. Needs the accessibility switch.</string>
    <string name="ona_overlay_backend_pc">PC / Wine bridge (TCP)</string>
    <string name="ona_overlay_backend_pc_summary">Keys, mouse and gamepad sent over Wi-Fi to pc-bridge/ona_bridge.py on the PC.</string>
    <string name="ona_overlay_backend_root">Root shell</string>
    <string name="ona_overlay_backend_root_summary">Keys and taps into any app with su (input keyevent / tap). Needs a rooted phone.</string>
    <string name="ona_overlay_host">PC address</string>
    <string name="ona_overlay_port">Port</string>
    <string name="ona_overlay_reconnect">Reconnect</string>
    <string name="ona_overlay_haptics">Vibrate on press</string>
    <string name="ona_overlay_how">How it works (battery)</string>
    <string name="ona_overlay_how_text">App detection uses the accessibility event that Android sends only when a window changes: no polling, no wake-ups. Without accessibility, usage access is read once per second and only while the screen is on. Controls redraw only while touched; each control is its own small window, so the rest of the screen goes straight to the app.</string>
    <string name="ona_overlay_a11y_label">ONA floating controls</string>
    <string name="ona_overlay_a11y_description">Lets ONA Controls show your floating controls when the app you picked is opened (it only looks at which app is in front), press keys in that app like a keyboard, and touch it for buttons you set to TAP. It does not read screen content.</string>
